<!--
    A 64-bit compare on a 32-bit target, and a long long stack parameter.

    The low words are compared (cmp) and the high words subtracted with that
    borrow (sbb); the result is read off the flags (setl, setb). Lifted, a
    signed compare is the XOR of SBORROW4(ahi,bhi), SBORROW4(ahi-bhi,c) and
    the sign of ahi-bhi-c, with c = alo < blo, and an unsigned one is
    ahi < bhi || ahi-bhi < c. kuna_borrowcompare folds either back into one
    compare of the two wholes, also with a declared prototype. With no
    prototype each long long arrived as two int parameters; option pairparam
    joins two stack words a borrow or carry links into one parameter.

    Built from this source with
      clang -target i386-linux-gnu -O2 -fno-inline -c t64.c
    (.text, 0xf1 bytes):
      long long add64(long long a, long long b) { return a + b; }
      int lt64(long long a, long long b) { return a < b; }
      int ltu64(unsigned long long a, unsigned long long b) { return a < b; }
      int eq64(long long a, long long b) { return a == b; }
      long long shl64(long long a, int n) { return a << n; }
      int lt_const(long long a) { return a < 100000LL; }
      long long pick(long long a, long long b) { return a < b ? b : a; }
-->
